<title>AUSTRIA: OPEC's top priority to keep current prices - Iran.</title>
<headline>OPEC's top priority to keep current prices - Iran.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iranian oil minister Gholamreza Aghazadeh said on Wednesday that OPEC's top priority was to try and keep oil prices at current high levels and the best way to do that was to maintain current output quotas.</p>
<p>&quot;I suppose for this meeting it is best for us to keep the current situation in the market,&quot; the minister told lobby reorters. &quot;If we want to keep at this (price) level it is best to keep the current ceiling.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;It depends on all of us being very careful,&quot; Aghazadeh added.</p>
</text>
